From da794094a69228f2c1e72b747b6268ff001ffd9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 11:36:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui: Traffic Analyzer - wedge-proof live polling, stalled
 indicator, history auto-refresh

The live view could freeze at its last paint while the browser kept
polling: getJSON() had no timeout and the in-flight guard was a boolean
cleared only in the readyState-4 callback, so one response that never
completed (httpd busy during an apply, a Wi-Fi roam, a sleep/resume
half-open connection) wedged the loop forever. Recovery required
leaving the page and coming back.

- getJSON(): rebuilt on onloadend (fires exactly once on success, HTTP
  error, timeout AND abort) + xhr.timeout = max(3000, 2*pollMs+2000) ms.
  Callback is now cb(data, ok); a non-200 or non-JSON response yields
  ok=false instead of an empty object.
- Live loop: the in-flight guard now holds the XHR + a start stamp, and
  a tick-side watchdog aborts any request older than
  max(5000, 2*pollMs+3000) ms - the loop always self-heals.
- Failed polls no longer render zeros: the page keeps its last paint and
  the status pill shows an amber dot + "No response" (new dict key
  RTRF_72, appended to all 25 dicts in lockstep) until polls answer.
- History windows (5 min / 24 h / 14 d / By month) now refresh every
  30 s; they were one-shot fetches that went permanently stale.

Server side exonerated: the CGI is a non-blocking tmpfs read and rtrafd
publishes live.json via atomic rename, so the freeze was client-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
